  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design pedagogy for analog-to-digital converters (ADCs): sampling and the Nyquist limit, quantization and resolution, and the four dominant architectures — SAR (successive approximation), flash (parallel), integrating (dual-slope), and sigma-delta (oversampling + noise shaping). Teaches how to select and design the right ADC for a given resolution/speed/power trade-off, building on comparator and analog-switch devices from semiconductor-devices and precision resistors from passive-components.",
